{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StudioFilesPanel",
  "$description": "The Navigator's Files tree, as a Jx document over the kit. `files/files.ts` keeps every decision — which directories are listed, which entries `.gitignore` masks, which rows the window draws, what a click on a row means, what the context menu offers and what each verb does to the filesystem — and hands this document one projection: a word saying which of three things to draw, a toolbar whose state is already resolved, and rows whose every field is already a string. Nothing here asks what a file is, how tall the Navigator is, or whether a directory has been read. The tree is a FLAT list and the DOM holds a window onto it, so the rows a `$map` renders are the visible slice: an expanded `node_modules` is eleven rows rather than ten thousand, and `aria-level` / `aria-posinset` / `aria-setsize` are what keep the ARIA true while it is. Four facts a row carries are bound against ONE scope field each — the selected path, the dragged path, the drop target and the roving tab stop — so moving the selection or dragging a file re-evaluates an attribute per drawn row instead of rebuilding the list under the reader's pointer. The pragmatic-drag-and-drop handles are an ISLAND: the document draws the rows and the tree, and the adapter attaches sources and targets to them through `onNodeCreated` (specs/studio-ui-guidelines.md §9.4).",
  "tagName": "div",
  "attributes": {
    "part": "files"
  },
  "style": {
    "$description": "What the twenty `.file-tree*`, `.files-toolbar`, `.project-header` and `.project-name` rules in `styles/panels.css` said, keyed on `part` and re-pointed at the studio token layer. Three names could not come with the declarations. The five `var(--spectrum-font-size-50 | -75, …)` reads are the kit's `--jx-text-sm` and `--jx-text-md`, which are the same 11px and 12px — a `--spectrum-*` name is declared by `<sp-theme>` and by nothing else in this package, so a document that reads one is a document whose type size changes when a component it does not use is removed. The `.selected`, `.dragging`, `.drag-over` and `.drag-over-root` classes are `data-` attributes on a part, because a part is the handle now and because a state a handler adds and forgets to take off is exactly the defect a cancelled drag used to leave on screen. And the row's indent was `padding-left:${8 + depth * 16}px` composed per row in TypeScript; it is a `--depth` custom property here, so the arithmetic that decides what a level LOOKS like lives with the rest of the styling.",
    "display": "flex",
    "flexDirection": "column",
    "height": "100%",
    "minHeight": "0",
    "overflow": "hidden",
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
    "color": "var(--fg)",
    "& [part=\"view-slot\"], & [part=\"header-slot\"], & [part=\"locale-slot\"]": {
      "$description": "A `$switch` renders its own container, and none of these three is a box: each stands exactly where its case does, so the case's own rule is the only one that lays anything out.",
      "display": "contents"
    },
    "& [part=\"empty\"]": {
      "$description": "The two states that are not a tree. They are two states and not one sentence: a window with no project at all and a monorepo root that has not been pointed at a site are different situations, and only the second has anything to offer (§11).",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-6)",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-4)"
    },
    "& [part=\"empty\"] p": {
      "margin": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"frame\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "height": "100%",
      "minHeight": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"project-header\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-3)",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-3) var(--jx-space-4)",
      "borderBottom": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "flexShrink": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"project-name\"]": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "overflow": "hidden",
      "textOverflow": "ellipsis",
      "whiteSpace": "nowrap"
    },
    "& [part=\"toolbar\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-2)",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-2) var(--jx-space-3)",
      "borderBottom": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "flexShrink": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"search\"]": {
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"tree\"]": {
      "$description": "The scroller as well as the list. `ui/virtual-window.ts` walks up from the element it is given looking for the nearest thing that scrolls, and finding itself is the shortest answer.",
      "flex": "1",
      "minHeight": "0",
      "overflowY": "auto"
    },
    "& [part=\"tree\"][data-drop=\"true\"]": {
      "background": "var(--hover-bg)"
    },
    "& [part=\"pad-top\"], & [part=\"pad-bottom\"]": {
      "$description": "The two spacers reserve the scroll height of the rows the window left out. They are `aria-hidden` because a `role=\"tree\"` owns `treeitem`s, and an empty div that exists to be four thousand pixels tall is not one.",
      "flexShrink": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"]": {
      "$description": "`block-size` is a CONTRACT, not a look: the tree is windowed, and a window can only reserve the right amount of scroll for the rows it did not draw if every row is the same known height. `--jx-control-h` is the kit's 24px — what the box already computed to — and it follows the density setting, which the hard-coded 24 could not. The renderer measures a real row anyway and believes the measurement over any declared number.",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-3)",
      "paddingInline": "calc(var(--jx-space-3) + var(--depth, 0) * 16px) var(--jx-space-3)",
      "blockSize": "var(--jx-control-h)",
      "boxSizing": "border-box",
      "cursor": "pointer",
      "color": "var(--fg)",
      "userSelect": "none",
      ":hover": {
        "background": "var(--hover-bg)"
      },
      ":focus-visible": {
        "$description": "Roving tabindex moves focus between rows, so the ring is the only thing telling a keyboard user where they are.",
        "outline": "var(--jx-focus-ring)",
        "outlineOffset": "-2px"
      }
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-selected=\"true\"]": {
      "background": "var(--accent-20)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-dragging=\"true\"]": {
      "opacity": "0.4"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-drop=\"true\"]": {
      "background": "var(--accent-20)",
      "outline": "1px solid var(--accent)",
      "outlineOffset": "-1px"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-loading=\"true\"]": {
      "$description": "A directory whose listing has not arrived yet. It holds the place and it is NOT a `treeitem`: the keyboard cannot land on it, the set counts do not include it, and it is replaced by the real rows on the repaint the listing provokes.",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "fontStyle": "italic",
      "cursor": "default"
    },
    "& [part=\"twisty\"]": {
      "$description": "A file has no case, so the box draws empty and keeps its width — which is what lines every name in the tree up whether or not its row can be opened.",
      "inlineSize": "14px",
      "flexShrink": "0",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "justifyContent": "center",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "--jx-icon-size": "12px"
    },
    "& [part=\"row-icon\"]": {
      "flexShrink": "0",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "--jx-icon-size": "16px"
    },
    "& [part=\"row-name\"]": {
      "overflow": "hidden",
      "textOverflow": "ellipsis",
      "whiteSpace": "nowrap",
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"locale\"]": {
      "$description": "The language chip. Deliberately declares no block size, no padding and no line height: the row above is one control-height by contract, and a chip that grew the box would desynchronise the window's scroll reservation from the height it reserves by. It only ever shrinks the text. A chip, not a filter term: the search matches the file's name alone, because a query that silently also matched a language would make “why is this file here” unanswerable from what is on screen.",
      "marginInlineStart": "auto",
      "flexShrink": "0",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-sm)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "overflow": "hidden",
      "textOverflow": "ellipsis",
      "whiteSpace": "nowrap",
      "maxInlineSize": "6em"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "tagName": "div",
      "attributes": {
        "part": "view-slot",
        "role": "none"
      },
      "$switch": {
        "$ref": "#/state/view"
      },
      "cases": {
        "none": {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "empty"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "No project loaded"
            }
          ]
        },
        "welcome": {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "empty"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "p",
              "textContent": "Open a project folder to get started."
            },
            {
              "tagName": "jx-button",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "open-project"
              },
              "$props": {
                "variant": "accent",
                "size": "sm"
              },
              "onclick": {
                "$prototype": "Function",
                "body": [
                  {
                    "operator": "call",
                    "target": {
                      "$ref": "#/state/openProject"
                    },
                    "value": []
                  }
                ],
                "description": "The declared `project.open` command, run through the registry — not a second opener of this surface's own. It is the one the chord, the palette and the status bar's PROJECT field already run, so a window that opens a project from here reports the outcome the same way they do (§12.5)."
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "span",
                  "textContent": "Open Project"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "tree": {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "frame"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "header-slot",
                "role": "none"
              },
              "$switch": {
                "$ref": "#/state/headerState"
              },
              "cases": {
                "shown": {
                  "tagName": "div",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "project-header"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "span",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "project-name",
                        "title": "${state.projectName}"
                      },
                      "textContent": "${state.projectName}"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "toolbar"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "jx-action-group",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "toolbar-actions"
                  },
                  "$props": {
                    "compact": true,
                    "label": "File tree actions"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "jx-action-button",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "new-file"
                      },
                      "$props": {
                        "size": "sm",
                        "icon": "plus",
                        "label": "New File",
                        "hint": "New File"
                      },
                      "onclick": {
                        "$prototype": "Function",
                        "body": [
                          {
                            "operator": "call",
                            "target": {
                              "$ref": "#/state/newFile"
                            },
                            "value": []
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "jx-action-button",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "refresh"
                      },
                      "$props": {
                        "size": "sm",
                        "icon": "arrows-clockwise",
                        "label": "Refresh",
                        "hint": "Refresh"
                      },
                      "onclick": {
                        "$prototype": "Function",
                        "body": [
                          {
                            "operator": "call",
                            "target": {
                              "$ref": "#/state/refresh"
                            },
                            "value": []
                          }
                        ],
                        "description": "The rules go with the listings. Refresh is what an author reaches for after editing a `.gitignore` by hand, and a tree that came back still hiding by the old rules would read as the button not having worked."
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "jx-action-button",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "show-ignored"
                      },
                      "$props": {
                        "size": "sm",
                        "icon": {
                          "$ref": "#/state/ignoredIcon"
                        },
                        "label": {
                          "$ref": "#/state/ignoredLabel"
                        },
                        "hint": {
                          "$ref": "#/state/ignoredLabel"
                        },
                        "selected": {
                          "$ref": "#/state/ignoredSelected"
                        }
                      },
                      "onclick": {
                        "$prototype": "Function",
                        "body": [
                          {
                            "operator": "call",
                            "target": {
                              "$ref": "#/state/toggleIgnored"
                            },
                            "value": []
                          }
                        ],
                        "description": "A repaint and nothing else: the ignored entries were never dropped from the cached listings, only from the rows built out of them."
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "jx-textfield",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "search"
                  },
                  "$props": {
                    "label": "Filter files",
                    "placeholder": "Filter files…",
                    "size": "sm",
                    "value": {
                      "$ref": "#/state/query"
                    }
                  },
                  "oninput": {
                    "$prototype": "Function",
                    "body": [
                      {
                        "operator": "call",
                        "target": {
                          "$ref": "#/state/search"
                        },
                        "value": [
                          {
                            "$ref": "event#/target/value"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ],
                    "description": "The query matches a file's NAME and nothing else. A directory is kept whatever it says, because hiding the folder a match sits in would leave the match with nowhere to be drawn."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "tree",
                "role": "tree",
                "aria-label": "Project files",
                "data-drop": "${state.rootDrop || null}"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "div",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "pad-top",
                    "aria-hidden": "true",
                    "style": "${state.padTop}"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "$prototype": "Array",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/state/rows"
                  },
                  "key": {
                    "$ref": "$map/item/key"
                  },
                  "map": {
                    "tagName": "div",
                    "attributes": {
                      "part": "row-slot",
                      "role": "none"
                    },
                    "$switch": {
                      "$ref": "$map/item/kind"
                    },
                    "cases": {
                      "item": {
                        "tagName": "div",
                        "attributes": {
                          "part": "row",
                          "role": "treeitem",
                          "style": "--depth:${$map.item.depth}",
                          "data-path": "${$map.item.path}",
                          "data-type": "${$map.item.type}",
                          "data-selected": "${state.selectedPath === $map.item.path ? 'true' : null}",
                          "data-dragging": "${state.dragPath === $map.item.path ? 'true' : null}",
                          "data-drop": "${state.dropPath === $map.item.path ? 'true' : null}",
                          "aria-level": "${$map.item.level}",
                          "aria-posinset": "${$map.item.posInSet}",
                          "aria-setsize": "${$map.item.setSize}",
                          "aria-expanded": "${$map.item.ariaExpanded || null}",
                          "tabindex": "${state.tabStopPath === $map.item.path ? '0' : '-1'}"
                        },
                        "onclick": {
                          "$prototype": "Function",
                          "body": [
                            {
                              "stopPropagation": true
                            },
                            {
                              "operator": "call",
                              "target": {
                                "$ref": "#/state/activate"
                              },
                              "value": [
                                {
                                  "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "description": "One verb for both kinds of row. What a click MEANS — expand this directory, open that file — is the flow's to decide, and a row that decided it here would be a second answer to it beside Enter's."
                        },
                        "oncontextmenu": {
                          "$prototype": "Function",
                          "body": [
                            {
                              "preventDefault": true
                            },
                            {
                              "stopPropagation": true
                            },
                            {
                              "operator": "call",
                              "target": {
                                "$ref": "#/state/contextMenu"
                              },
                              "value": [
                                {
                                  "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                },
                                {
                                  "$ref": "event#/clientX"
                                },
                                {
                                  "$ref": "event#/clientY"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "onkeydown": {
                          "$prototype": "Function",
                          "body": [
                            {
                              "$switch": {
                                "$ref": "event#/key"
                              },
                              "cases": {
                                "ArrowDown": [
                                  {
                                    "preventDefault": true
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "operator": "call",
                                    "target": {
                                      "$ref": "#/state/moveFocus"
                                    },
                                    "value": [
                                      {
                                        "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                      },
                                      1
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ],
                                "ArrowUp": [
                                  {
                                    "preventDefault": true
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "operator": "call",
                                    "target": {
                                      "$ref": "#/state/moveFocus"
                                    },
                                    "value": [
                                      {
                                        "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                      },
                                      -1
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ],
                                "ArrowRight": [
                                  {
                                    "preventDefault": true
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "operator": "call",
                                    "target": {
                                      "$ref": "#/state/expandRow"
                                    },
                                    "value": [
                                      {
                                        "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ],
                                "ArrowLeft": [
                                  {
                                    "preventDefault": true
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "operator": "call",
                                    "target": {
                                      "$ref": "#/state/collapseRow"
                                    },
                                    "value": [
                                      {
                                        "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ],
                                "Enter": [
                                  {
                                    "preventDefault": true
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "operator": "call",
                                    "target": {
                                      "$ref": "#/state/activate"
                                    },
                                    "value": [
                                      {
                                        "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            }
                          ],
                          "description": "The keyboard is bound to the ROW rather than to the tree, so which row a key is about is the row's own `$map` item and never a lookup. ↑ and ↓ step through the MODEL: the step can land on a row the window did not draw, and moving the scroller and letting the focus follow the repaint is the flow's answer to that. A key with no case here is not prevented, so typeahead, Tab and Home reach the browser."
                        },
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "tagName": "div",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "twisty",
                              "aria-hidden": "true"
                            },
                            "$switch": {
                              "$ref": "$map/item/twisty"
                            },
                            "cases": {
                              "expanded": {
                                "tagName": "jx-icon",
                                "$props": {
                                  "name": "caret-down"
                                }
                              },
                              "collapsed": {
                                "tagName": "jx-icon",
                                "$props": {
                                  "name": "caret-right"
                                }
                              }
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "tagName": "jx-icon",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "row-icon",
                              "aria-hidden": "true"
                            },
                            "$props": {
                              "name": {
                                "$ref": "$map/item/icon"
                              }
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "tagName": "span",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "row-name"
                            },
                            "textContent": "${$map.item.name}"
                          },
                          {
                            "tagName": "div",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "locale-slot",
                              "role": "none"
                            },
                            "$switch": {
                              "$ref": "$map/item/localeState"
                            },
                            "cases": {
                              "shown": {
                                "tagName": "span",
                                "attributes": {
                                  "part": "locale"
                                },
                                "textContent": "${$map.item.locale}"
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "loading": {
                        "tagName": "div",
                        "attributes": {
                          "part": "row",
                          "role": "none",
                          "data-loading": "true",
                          "style": "--depth:${$map.item.depth}"
                        },
                        "textContent": "Loading…"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "div",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "pad-bottom",
                    "aria-hidden": "true",
                    "style": "${state.padBottom}"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
